  "version": "enrolled",
  "operative_text": "(a_in_person_id) not stated.\n(b_no_id_remedy) not stated.\n(c_mail_ballot_id) not stated.\n(d_proof_of_citizenship) not stated.\n(e_other_rule)\n(section) R.C. 3503.15(A)(2)(a)\n(quote) State agencies, including, but not limited to, the department of health, bureau of motor vehicles, department of job and family services, and the department of rehabilitation and corrections, shall provide any information and data to the secretary of state that is collected in the course of normal business and that is necessary to register to vote, to update an elector's registration, or to maintain the statewide voter registration database established pursuant to this section, except where prohibited by federal law or regulation.\n(section) R.C. 3503.15(C)(4)\n(quote) A search program capable of verifying registered voters and their registration information by name, driver's license number, birth date, social security number, or current address;\n(section) R.C. 3503.15(D)(7)\n(quote) Establishing a uniform method for addressing instances in which records contained in the statewide voter registration database do not conform with records maintained by an agency, state, or group of states described in division (A)(2)(a) or (3)(a) of this section. That method shall prohibit an elector's voter registration from being canceled on the sole basis that the information in the registration record does not conform to records maintained by such an agency.\n(section) R.C. 3503.11\n(quote) The registrar shall send any completed registration application received at the bureau of motor vehicles headquarters location and any completed change of residence or change of name form processed electronically in systems or programs operated and maintained by the bureau of motor vehicles to the secretary of state within five days after accepting the application or other form.\n(other) R.C. 3503.11: BMV sends completed voter registration forms to the Secretary of State within five days; BMV reports declined and completed counts\n(other) R.C. 3503.15: statewide voter registration database; agencies share data; confidentiality and no sale of the data; method for records that do not match agency records\n(other) R.C. 3503.18: Department of Health death reports monthly, plus a supplemental report within one month of late notice\n(other) R.C. 3503.21: cancellation of registration (conforming change)\n(other) R.C. 3506.22: lowers the minimum number of direct recording electronic voting machines\n(other) version: 00_IN: database and BMV data text only; no ID or citizenship text\n(other) version: 01_RS: adds BMV transmission content and format, confidentiality rules for shared data, supplemental death reports; no ID or citizenship text\n(other) version: 02_PS: same, no ID or citizenship text\n(other) version: 03_RH: same, no ID or citizenship text\n(other) version: 04_PH: same, no ID or citizenship text\n(other) version: 05_EN: same, no ID or citizenship text\n(other) note: No in-person ID, no-ID remedy, mail-ballot ID or citizenship text in any version. Slot e records the BMV and agency data-matching rules, including a bar on cancelling a registration on the sole basis of a mismatch. The enrolled text prints these sections in clean form (the 2013 file appears to show no struck words in the quoted passages). Vote mapping per brief: Senate passage on 01_RS, House passage on 03_RH; the table-amendment votes are on floor amendments whose text I do not have. ID flag is false on passage votes because the bill has no ID text in any version.\n(note) Off this topic: the bill sets no ID or citizenship-proof rule.",
